{"skill":{"slug":"playwright-scraper-skill","displayName":"Playwright Scraper Skill"},"version":{"version":"1.2.0","createdAt":1770470666815,"changelog":"Initial ClawHub release: Pure Playwright with anti-bot protection, bilingual docs (EN/ZH), successfully tested on Discuss.com.hk","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","size":1625,"sha256":"124b12f49a5abe7d36177bc7d9c873bea78c419cf238e573247e43a494abad2d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","size":3011,"sha256":"84e39b85a36f685e1633860144b345d065a2da6d5aee31e9a74382aef17d8b15","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"INSTALL.md","size":2203,"sha256":"8a9cbfe21c4aabb457ddd0a2ab6514dfcb2d0cb825ee3d42ccc1d700e66b4c27","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README.md","size":4471,"sha256":"eeb306a0f6842460c80331b44375f201a463e10d93d72413a5448e4c23d536de","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README_ZH.md","size":4267,"sha256":"8d440826643b5ee25c769903594e52d4d4a15e23887b8d784ac46efe8d505221","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6155,"sha256":"c2f4ec84a3a054712dbf9e192be22250d87bffff8906ddbdacea7a3c8b3cfb26","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/README.md","size":4207,"sha256":"5dcca9d3116a606988b12fa855b0d9c4dc12e918bb7f4937f61830b8d6ef0a96","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/discuss-hk.sh","size":432,"sha256":"44846b58553d273afbaf36dcb203b81987058421b443ca699fc38d3bb160e0ff","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"package-lock.json","size":1696,"sha256":"1b49631e50bb04852b21c00cbacbf83e7a5d50ec390806309fbf0e715bf14e65","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"package.json","size":531,"sha256":"371e3356019ab665f035fb89fe22c9221d3893ccaf712c9484d738ad6be0453e","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/playwright-simple.js","size":1755,"sha256":"97a8a7cfd0f96e7f4d7b8047f34f18f8494f63d1e044c4bfee93b36d1b510141","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/playwright-stealth.js","size":5572,"sha256":"b0eef508b8d56321da7bb00b77513286f9dd84500eb032e0d7ade1fa4890ba00","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"test.sh","size":1110,"sha256":"f07de4f7807a6fbf3c0609c21d6b3184f0896fb6e50931eb333ad4b0188a2637","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2610,"sha256":"50d14788119618b8c573f81aae38e4922f4dfa4b2aabfc8775722b8289510911","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789038255445,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"bbee115c2945a67792a732b86002b274cc04cc4612c6ffe1c110568f50db0282","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/bbee115c2945a67792a732b86002b274cc04cc4612c6ffe1c110568f50db0282","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: playwright-scraper-skill\nVersion: 1.2.0\n\nThe skill is designed for web scraping, including bypassing anti-bot measures using Playwright. While the core functionality and documentation are aligned with its stated purpose, the `scripts/playwright-stealth.js` file uses the `--no-sandbox` and `--disable-setuid-sandbox` flags when launching Chromium. Disabling the browser's sandbox is a security risk, as it can make the system more vulnerable if the browser itself is compromised by malicious web content. Although this is a common practice in web scraping for compatibility, it represents a risky capability without clear malicious intent from the skill author, thus classifying it as suspicious.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162024249},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":35,"checkedAt":1789038255445},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a disclosed web-scraping skill, but its stealth mode weakens browser protections and gives broad scraping and file-saving power without enough safeguards.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The stealth script launches Chromium with --no-sandbox, --disable-setuid-sandbox, and disabled site isolation while visiting arbitrary websites, which is disproportionate for routine scraping and increases host compromise impact if a browser exploit is encountered.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation uses npm and Playwright with a lockfile present, but documentation repeatedly uses unpinned npx commands and optionally tells users to install and run a separate deep-scraper skill without pinning or audit-boundary warnings.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Instructions recommend stealth scraping for Cloudflare/403 cases and suggest proxies, future cookies, and CAPTCHA handling, but do not clearly require authorization, legal/ToS review, privacy handling, or target allowlisting.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No system persistence, credential theft, or background service was found, but the scripts can write screenshots and optional HTML to caller-controlled paths and the stealth script saves screenshots by default, which is broader local file mutation than necessary without path containment.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is Playwright web scraping with anti-bot/stealth behavior, and the scripts do implement that purpose. The concern is that arbitrary URL navigation, anti-bot evasion, screenshot/HTML capture, and default stealth use create high-impact misuse and host-network exposure without meaningful scoping or warnings.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you need this exact scraping capability and can run it in an isolated environment. Use it only on sites you are authorized to access, avoid authenticated or sensitive pages, keep screenshot/HTML outputs in a dedicated directory, and do not follow the optional deep-scraper install path unless you separately review and pin that dependency.","findings":"[TP4] expected: The anti-bot and stealth claims are broadly consistent with the actual code that changes user agent and hides webdriver; I downgraded this from deception to an under-disclosed risk because the purpose is explicit.\n[AE1] unexpected: The referenced stealth script was present in the artifact and fully inspected, so this coverage concern is not retained as an independent issue.\n[TM1] expected: The rm command is limited to predictable temporary test outputs and screenshots in a test cleanup script; it does not support a malicious or high-impact finding.\n[RP1] unexpected: Dependency installation is expected, but unpinned npx usage and an unpinned optional external skill install are real supply-chain concerns users should review.\n[SQP-2] expected: Stealth scraping and page capture are core advertised features, but the artifacts under-disclose authorization, privacy, and retention risks for saved screenshots and HTML.\n[LP3] unexpected: The skill needs browser and script execution, but it does not define a clear permission boundary or target scope, which compounds the arbitrary-navigation risk.\n[T05] expected: Arbitrary URL navigation is expected for a scraper, but the lack of URL, redirect, and private-network restrictions creates a material SSRF-style exposure from the agent host.\n[T09] unexpected: Disabling Chromium sandboxing and site isolation is not adequately justified and materially increases risk when visiting arbitrary or hostile pages; unrestricted output paths are also a lower-severity file overwrite concern.\n[T08] unexpected: The YouTube transcript workflow installs and executes an unpinned external skill, which is optional but outside the reviewed artifact and not adequately bounded.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789038255445}}}}}